  "description": "CMID (Contrastive Mask Image Distillation) is a unified self-supervised learning framework for remote sensing image understanding, combining contrastive learning and masked image modeling in a teacher-student self-distillation architecture. It is architecture-agnostic and effective for both CNNs and ViTs, learning representations with both global semantic separability and local spatial perceptibility.",
